lpac 2.3.0 pcsc driver: fix reader selection so multi-reader hosts work.

Upstream pcsc_open_hCard_iter has two defects that together make lpac usable only
on the FIRST PC/SC reader of a host:

  1. LPAC_APDU_PCSC_DRV_NAME alone is never honoured: the name filter is evaluated
     only inside the "interface id set and mismatched" branch, so with just the name
     set lpac silently connects to reader index 0 (on this gateway that is a modem's
     virtual VPCD slot, not the card the caller asked for -> "euicc_init" failures).
  2. LPAC_APDU_PCSC_DRV_IFID=N (N != first index) crashes: the mismatch branch calls
     strstr(reader, getenv(ENV_DRV_NAME)) with a NULL needle when the name env is not
     set -> segmentation fault.

Make the two selectors independent: an explicit interface id selects exactly that
index; a name filter (substring match, as upstream intended) applies on its own.

--- a/driver/apdu/pcsc.c
+++ b/driver/apdu/pcsc.c
@@ -117,11 +117,13 @@
     DWORD dwActiveProtocol;

     const int id = getenv_or_default(ENV_DRV_IFID, (int)-1);
     if (id != -1 && id != index) {
-        const char *part_name = getenv(ENV_DRV_NAME);
-        if (strstr(reader, part_name) == NULL) {
-            return 0;
-        }
+        return 0; // an explicit interface id selects exactly one reader
+    }
+
+    const char *part_name = getenv(ENV_DRV_NAME);
+    if (part_name != NULL && strstr(reader, part_name) == NULL) {
+        return 0; // reader name filter did not match this reader
     }

     if (is_ignored_reader_name(reader)) {
